From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: jz4780: fix NULL dereference in tx_status after terminate

jz4780_dma_tx_status() compares the cookie with jzchan->desc without
checking that a descriptor is active. After the channel has been stopped
(terminate_all on an ALSA stop/xrun), desc is NULL, and ALSA's prepare ->
sync_stop -> dmaengine_tx_status() path then oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 00000000
  epc : jz4780_dma_tx_status+0x144
    snd_dmaengine_pcm_sync_stop
    snd_soc_pcm_component_sync_stop
    snd_pcm_do_prepare

Seen on the X1000 (HiFi Walker H2) whenever a playback stream underran
and was re-prepared. Check desc before dereferencing it.

Signed-off-by: Fathom
---
diff -Naur a/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c b/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
--- a/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
@@ -658,7 +658,7 @@
 		/* On the issued list, so hasn't been processed yet */
 		residue = jz4780_dma_desc_residue(jzchan,
 					to_jz4780_dma_desc(vdesc), 0);
-	} else if (cookie == jzchan->desc->vdesc.tx.cookie) {
+	} else if (jzchan->desc && cookie == jzchan->desc->vdesc.tx.cookie) {
 		residue = jz4780_dma_desc_residue(jzchan, jzchan->desc,
 					jzchan->curr_hwdesc + 1);
 	}
